  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Mirce">Mirce</ref> 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-h">Ceorles wergyld is on Myrcna lage CC scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-d">Ceorles wergild is on Myrcna lage CC scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1" corresp="#wit-q">Ceorles weregildum est in Mircenorum laga CC sol.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-d">In the law of the Mercians a <hi rend="italic">ceorl's</hi> wergild is 200 shillings</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin" corresp="#wit-h">According to the law of the Mercians, a layman's wergild is two hundred shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Eines Gemeinfreien Wergeld ist in Mercier-Recht (Land Ld) 200 Schill. [3⅓ Pfund].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">A ceorl's wergild is by Mercian law (in the Mercian land, Ld) 200 shillings [3⅓ pounds].</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Column O holds the Quadripartitus. Liebermann compares Norðleod 6.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
